{
  "summary": "This study investigates closed nanopores in silicon-carbon anodes as stress-regulation units to mitigate lithiation-induced deformation and interphase degradation. By engineering heteroatom-doped carbon hosts with abundant closed pores, the research redirects expansion stress inward, suppresses electrode swelling, and enhances Li+ kinetics. The nitrogen-doped composite achieves 1756.5 mAh g-1 reversible capacity, 90.2% initial Coulombic efficiency, and 868.4 mAh g-1 at 3 C, with reduced expansion from 38.4% to 13.1% after 50 cycles. The approach demonstrates scalability for practical battery anodes.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Closed nanopores in heteroatom-doped carbon hosts redirect lithiation-induced stress inward, suppressing electrode swelling",
    "Nitrogen-doped silicon-carbon composites achieve 1756.5 mAh g-1 reversible capacity and 868.4 mAh g-1 at 3 C",
    "The design reduces electrode thickness expansion from 38.4% to 13.1% after 50 cycles and enables scalable production"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes closed-pore stress regulation as a scalable structural strategy for practical low-expansion silicon-carbon anodes, addressing key limitations in high-energy lithium-ion battery electrodes."
}

{
  "summary": "This study integrated single-cell epigenomic data from 2.5 million adult mouse brain nuclei, profiling four histone modifications, transcriptomes, chromatin accessibility, DNA methylation, and 3D genome organization. The resulting atlas identified 100+ brain cell subclasses and defined active, primed, and repressive chromatin states across 81% of the genome. Active states with combinatorial histone marks better predict functional enhancers than accessibility alone, while H3K27me3 and H3K9me3 define repressive states. The resource enables deep learning models for predicting cell-type-specific epigenomic features and gene expression from DNA sequences.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The atlas spans over 100 brain cell subclasses using integrated epigenomic profiling",
    "Active chromatin states marked by combinatorial histone modifications better predict functional enhancers than chromatin accessibility alone",
    "H3K27me3- and H3K9me3-marked chromatin states delineate distinct modes of cell-type-specific gene repression"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This multimodal resource provides a comprehensive framework for annotating the brain regulatory genome and interpreting non-coding disease risk variants through cell-type-specific epigenomic features."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates a dual-copper catalytic system enabling switchable chlorine atom transfer radical reactions. The approach uses a dinuclear copper complex to activate unactivated alkyl chlorides and a mononuclear copper catalyst for controlled C-Cl bond reconstruction. The reaction switches between atom transfer radical addition (ATRA) and atom transfer radical polymerization (ATRP) modes depending on catalyst presence. Key applications include synthesizing diverse ATRA products and α-end-functionalized polyacrylates, with potential for direct PVC modification under mild conditions.",
  "key_findings": [
    "A dinuclear copper complex selectively activates unactivated alkyl chlorides for C-Cl bond cleavage",
    "Mononuclear copper catalyst mediates controllable C-Cl bond reconstruction",
    "Switchable reaction pathway between ATRA and ATRP modes based on catalyst presence"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a versatile platform for chlorine atom transfer radical reactions using unactivated alkyl chlorides, advancing synthetic strategies for functionalized small molecules and polymers."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated how protein kinase A (PKA) signaling regulates group 3 innate lymphoid cell (ILC3) homeostasis and IL-23-driven gut inflammation. Using a single-cell atlas, researchers found that prostaglandin activates PKA to promote tissue-protective functions, while IL-23 suppresses PKA inhibitors like PRKAR1A. Deletion of Prkar1a reduced ILC3s and increased infection susceptibility in mice. IL-23 overproduction decreased PRKAR1A, increasing PKA signaling and causing gut inflammation. Human ILC3s express PRKAR1A, which is downregulated by IL-23 or in inflammatory bowel disease.",
  "key_findings": [
    "IL-23 suppresses PKA inhibitors (PRKAR1A) in ILC3s",
    "Prkar1a deletion reduced ILC3 numbers and increased enteric infection susceptibility in mice",
    "IL-23 overproduction decreased PRKAR1A, increasing PKA signaling and gut inflammation"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes PKA signaling as a critical regulator of ILC3 homeostasis, revealing how IL-23 disrupts this balance to drive intestinal inflammation through PRKAR1A modulation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the emergence of a Chern metal in frustrated moiré Kondo lattices using angle-aligned MoTe2/WSe2 bilayers. It identifies a compressible state with nearly quantized Hall resistance and finite longitudinal resistance, indicating a bad metallic bulk. Nonlocal transport and magnetic circular dichroism confirm chiral edge states and a magnetization plateau before Kondo breakdown.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Observation of a compressible Chern metal at the onset of magnetic Kondo breakdown in MoTe2/WSe2 bilayers",
    "Nearly quantized Hall resistance and finite longitudinal resistance indicating a bad metallic bulk",
    "Magnetization plateau preceding Kondo breakdown, confirmed by magnetic circular dichroism"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study demonstrates how moiré engineering can stabilize Chern metals through the interplay of band topology and K. interactions, providing a pathway for designing exotic quantum phases."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates kinetic-environmental coupling at buried interfaces in ambient flexible perovskite solar cells. Using dual-side in situ photoluminescence, it reveals simultaneous nucleation at gas-liquid and liquid-solid interfaces during antisolvent processing. Outward solvent evaporation delays α-phase conversion at the buried interface, exacerbating moisture attack. The researchers designed a self-segregating molecule (NFA) that enriches at the buried interface to synchronize crystallization, passivate defects, and form a hydrophobic barrier. This approach achieved record power-conversion efficiencies of 24.84% and 21.46% on mini-modules while maintaining 96.26% efficiency after 1000h damp aging at 85±5% RH.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Simultaneous nucleation occurs at both gas-liquid and liquid-solid interfaces during antisolvent processing",
    "Outward solvent evaporation delays α-phase conversion at the buried interface, exacerbating moisture attack",
    "Self-segregating molecule NFA synchronizes crystallization, passivates defects, and forms a hydrophobic barrier"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes self-segregated interfacial regulation as a rational strategy to resolve kinetic-environmental coupling in ambient flexible perovskite solar cells, enabling high-performance devices with enhanced stability."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how early human settlement in the Arabian desert was influenced by stone availability alongside water. Using a 1,500-km geoarchaeological survey across Rub' al Khali, researchers found no lithic artefacts or knappable materials where freshwater existed but stone was scarce. Spatial analysis indicates settlement required both water and stone resources, with 57% of water-accessible terrain lacking suitable stone. This challenges models that prioritize water alone for predicting human dispersal.",
  "key_findings": [
    "No lithic artefacts or knappable raw materials were found in areas with abundant freshwater but scarce stone",
    "57% of water-accessible terrain lacks knappable stone, indicating stone availability as a critical constraint",
    "Settlement patterns co-occurred with water and lithic resources, not water alone, across multiple continents"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The findings demonstrate that stone resource availability, not water, was a key constraint on early human dispersal into arid regions, refining models of Pleistocene human migration."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated the impact of scientific publishing practices on journal quality and research dissemination. By analyzing trends in high-impact journals across multiple disciplines, the authors assessed how publication frequency, open access policies, and peer review efficiency influence scientific output. The findings indicate that journals with robust peer review systems and transparent data sharing protocols demonstrate higher research quality and broader societal impact, suggesting that standardized quality metrics could enhance scientific communication.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Journals with rigorous peer review and transparent data sharing protocols exhibit higher research quality",
    "Increased publication frequency correlates with greater research dissemination but may compromise quality",
    "Standardized quality metrics improve scientific communication and societal impact"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study provides evidence that structured quality assessment frameworks in scientific publishing can enhance research reliability and accessibility, contributing to more effective knowledge transfer across disciplines."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates amorphization of organic small molecules to enhance active site exposure in aqueous ammonium-ion batteries. By disrupting π-π stacking in tetraamino-dihydrophenazine (TDT), the approach improved electrolyte accessibility and activated buried redox sites. The amorphous TDT achieved high capacity retention (87.1% after 817 cycles) and demonstrated practical Ah-level performance in pouch cells, indicating durable, high-capacity aqueous ammonium-ion batteries.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Amorphous TDT achieved 242.8 mAh g-1 capacity at 0.1 A g-1",
    "Retained 87.1% capacity after 817 cycles (2900 h) with high surface area (738 m2 g-1)",
    "TDT||CuFe-PBA full cell maintained 100% capacity over 100,000 cycles at 5 A g-1"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "Amorphization of organic small molecules enables high-capacity, long-cycle aqueous ammonium-ion batteries by activating buried redox sites through disrupted molecular stacking."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates spin injection from a compensated magnet (Mn5Si3) without net magnetization, using lateral spin-valve devices to detect spin currents. Time-reversal symmetry breaking was demonstrated via switching magnetic states, showing spin polarization of 6.5-10% and diffusion lengths of 50-130 nm. The findings reveal altermagnetic order enables spintronic functionality without conventional magnetization.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Spin injection from Mn5Si3, a compensated magnet with zero net magnetization",
    "Time-reversal symmetry breaking observed through magnetic state switching",
    "Spin polarizations of 6.5-10% and diffusion lengths of 50-130 nm"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides experimental evidence that compensated magnets can generate spin currents via altermagnetic order, advancing spintronic applications without requiring net magnetization."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the role of lipids beyond structural components in brain cell functionality. It explores how specific lipid types contribute to cellular diversity and organization. The research indicates lipids actively participate in these processes, challenging the traditional view of lipids as passive structural elements. This finding highlights lipids' dynamic role in neural cell architecture.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Lipids are central players in cell diversity and organization",
    "Lipids actively participate in brain cell functionality",
    "Lipids challenge the traditional view of being passive structural elements"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates lipids' active role in neural cell organization, expanding understanding of lipid functions beyond structural roles in cellular systems."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates shear alignment polymer extrusion (SHAPE) 3D printing for fabricating high-loading nanocomposites with ordered nanostructures. By applying high shear forces during extrusion, the method aligns nanofillers like boron nitride nanosheets and carbon nanotubes in polymer matrices. The approach enables scalable production of complex 3D architectures with 55 wt% boron nitride in polylactic acid, achieving zero volume shrinkage and exceptional thermal stability. Vertically aligned structures show enhanced thermal conductivity (1.07 W/m/K), while horizontally aligned ones provide thermal insulation (0.071 W/m/K).",
  "key_findings": [
    "SHAPE 3D printing aligns high-loading nanofillers (e.g., 55 wt% boron nitride) in polymer matrices",
    "Printed composites exhibit zero volume shrinkage and thermal stability above polymer melting temperatures",
    "Vertically aligned structures achieve thermal conductivity of 1.07 W/m/K, while horizontally aligned ones offer thermal insulation of 0.071 W/m/K"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This method enables scalable fabrication of nanocomposites with tailored nanoscale order and macroscopic functionality, advancing cross-scale design for thermal management and structural applications."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates presynaptic homeostasis mechanisms by identifying vesicular SNARE protein VAMP7 as a key regulator. High-frequency stimulation triggers VAMP7-mediated inhibition of P/Q-type calcium channels, reducing neurotransmitter release. The mechanism involves activity-dependent delivery of VAMP7 to AP-3-derived vesicles, where it associates with syntaxin to modulate synaptic transmission. This process maintains neural circuit stability during adaptive plasticity.",
  "key_findings": [
    "VAMP7 reduces neurotransmitter release by inhibiting P/Q-type presynaptic calcium channels",
    "VAMP7 localizes to AP-3-derived synaptic vesicles activated by high-frequency stimulation",
    "VAMP7 deficiency increases FOS+ neurons by several fold, indicating homeostatic regulation of excitatory synapses"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The discovery of VAMP7-mediated presynaptic homeostasis provides a mechanism for activity-dependent synaptic stability, revealing how neural circuits maintain responsiveness during plasticity without postsynaptic receptor involvement."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether MnF2 exhibits altermagnetism using polarized inelastic neutron scattering (INS). The research identifies a magnon band splitting due to long-range dipolar coupling and a nonzero chirality in the neutron scattering cross section that reverses sign between magnon modes. These findings confirm MnF.2 as an altermagnet, demonstrating polarized INS's utility for characterizing altermagnets through magnon spectral fine structure.",
  "key_findings": [
    "MnF2 shows magnon band splitting from long-range dipolar coupling",
    "Neutron scattering cross section exhibits nonzero chirality reversing sign between magnon modes",
    "Polarized INS confirms MnF2 as an altermagnet through magnon spectral fine structure"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides direct spectroscopic evidence for altermagnetism in MnF2, highlighting polarized neutron scattering's capability to resolve magnon band splitting and chirality signatures essential for identifying altermagnets."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the long-standing challenge of achieving stable photocatalytic pure water splitting over Ta3N5 by identifying incompatibility in cocatalysts between alkaline water oxidation systems and pure water splitting as a critical bottleneck. The researchers developed a highly dispersed RuCoOx cocatalyst using a multi-step incipient wetness impregnation strategy. The optimized Pt@Cr2O3/Ta3N5/RuCoOx system achieved stoichiometric pure water splitting with an apparent quantum yield of 0.72% at 420 nm, the highest reported for Ta-based nitride/oxynitride photocatalysts. Mechanistic insights indicate enhanced interfacial electric fields and reduced reaction barriers improve hole extraction and surface kinetics.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Identification of cocatalyst incompatibility between alkaline water oxidation and pure water splitting as a bottleneck for Ta3N5 photocatalysis",
    "Development of a highly dispersed RuCoOx cocatalyst via multi-step incipient wetness impregnation",
    "Optimized Pt@Cr2O3/Ta3N5/RuCoOx achieves 0.72% apparent quantum yield for stoichiometric pure water splitting at 420 nm"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes cocatalyst compatibility as a fundamental design principle for stable photocatalytic water splitting in nitride and oxynitride materials, providing mechanistic insights for advancing solar-driven water splitting technologies."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how BAF chromatin remodeling complexes influence 3D chromatin architecture by disrupting BAF function via pharmacological inhibition and ARID1A deletion. It found increased accessibility at CTCF sites, elevated CTCF and SMC3 occupancy, and restructured 3D genome organization with strengthened topological domain boundaries and shorter promoter-proximal loops. These changes indicate an antagonistic relationship between BAF and CTCF-cohesin complexes.",
  "key_findings": [
    "BAF loss increases accessibility at CTCF-binding sites",
    "CTCF and SMC3 occupancy rises following BAF disruption",
    "3D genome restructuring with strengthened topological domain boundaries and shorter promoter-proximal loops"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The findings reveal a direct antagonistic relationship between BAF chromatin remodeling complexes and CTCF-cohesin complexes, providing mechanistic insight into how chromatin architecture is dynamically regulated."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how skin barrier function is maintained through interactions between immune cells, microbes, and epidermal stem cells. Using mice, researchers identified that Langerh. cells produce prostaglandin E2 to regulate stem cell proliferation and differentiation, ensuring barrier integrity. Disruption of this pathway causes stem cell overactivation and barrier weakening. The microbial environment modulates this immune-epithelial feedback loop, providing a mechanism for adaptive skin homeostasis.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Langerhans cells produce prostaglandin E2 to restrain stem cell proliferation and promote epidermal differentiation",
    "Disruption of the prostaglandin E2 pathway leads to stem cell overactivation and compromised barrier function",
    "The local microbial environment tunes Langerhans cell activity in a rheostat-like mechanism to maintain skin barrier homeostasis"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a microbial-immune-epithelial feedback loop that dynamically regulates skin barrier integrity through stem cell dynamics, offering a general mechanism for adaptive homeostasis in barrier tissues."
}

{
  "summary": "This study quantifies magnetic interactions in Fe3GeTe2/graphite/Fe3GeTe2 heterostructures using cross-sectional Lorentz transmission electron microscopy and off-axis electron holography. It measures local projected magnetic induction within layers, revealing domain alignment weakens with increasing separation, yielding a stray-field coupling length scale of 37±7 nm. This corresponds to a 23% reduction in interlayer magnetic induction relative to bulk FGT and a near-surface reduction up to ∼100 nm.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Domain alignment weakens with increasing FGT separation, yielding a stray-field coupling length scale of : 37±7 nm",
    "This length scale corresponds to a 23% reduction in interlayer magnetic induction relative to bulk FGT",
    "Magnetic induction reduces relative to bulk FGT up to ∼100 nm from a surface"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study provides quantitative characterization of magnetic coupling in stacked van der Waals magnets, establishing a critical length scale for interlayer interactions that informs device design."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates pharmacological inhibition of METTL1, a tRNA methyltransferase, as a potential anti-cancer strategy. Using STM9005, a selective METTL1 inhibitor, the researchers demonstrated reduced cancer cell growth, differentiation changes, and cell cycle dysregulation across multiple malignancies. In vivo, inhibition impaired tumor growth and prolonged survival in mouse models. The findings suggest targeting tRNA methylation could be a viable therapeutic approach for aggressive cancers.",
  "key_findings": [
    "STM9005 selectively inhibits METTL1, reducing m7G modifications on specific tRNAs",
    "Inhibition caused decreased cancer cell proliferation and differentiation changes across multiple cancer types",
    "In vivo treatment significantly reduced tumor growth and improved survival in mouse cancer models"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes pharmacological targeting of tRNA methylation as a viable therapeutic strategy for multiple aggressive malignancies, providing proof of concept for inhibiting oncogenic tRNA modifications."
}

{
  "summary": "This study examines the reliability of AI-generated mathematical proofs as AI systems increasingly produce mathematical breakthroughs. The research assesses whether AI proofchecking mechanisms can be trusted to validate complex mathematical arguments without human oversight. The findings indicate significant concerns about the accuracy and trustworthiness of AI-generated proofs in high-stakes mathematical contexts.",
  "key_findings": [
    "AI proofchecking systems show reliability issues when validating complex mathematical proofs",
    "AI-generated mathematical breakthroughs raise questions about proof validation accuracy",
    "Trust in AI proofchecking mechanisms is compromised in high-stakes mathematical contexts"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work highlights critical challenges in ensuring the accuracy of AI-generated mathematical proofs, contributing to the broader understanding of trustworthiness in automated proof validation systems."
}

{
  "summary": "This review examines aluminum scandium nitride (AlScN) as a semiconductor with enhanced ferroelectric and piezoelectric properties due to scandium incorporation into aluminum nitride. It addresses challenges in high-quality epitaxial film growth, including ferroelectric endurance issues, interface instability, and leakage currents. The study highlights recent advances in AlScN applications for ferroelectric memories, radio-frequency circuits, and high-electron-mobility transistors, emphasizing potential for energy-efficient computing and AI hardware.",
  "key_findings": [
    "AlScN demonstrates improved ferroelectric switching and piezoelectric responses compared to pure AlN",
    "High Sc content in epitaxial films faces challenges like reduced ferroelectric endurance and interface instability",
    "Recent AlScN applications include ferroelectric memories, radio-frequency circuits, and high-electron-mobility transistors"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This review establishes AlScN's potential to enable energy-efficient computing and sensing hardware through optimized ferroelectric and piezoelectric properties, advancing next-generation AI systems."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated whether dysregulated mRNA splicing in lupus neutrophils generates neoantigens recognized by T and B cells. Using mass spectrometry and T/B cell co-culture, researchers identified 21 splicing-derived peptides presented by MHC-I in SLE patients. These peptides triggered interferon-γ secretion, clonal T cell expansion, and autoantatic IgG antibodies, indicating splicing errors drive lupus autoimmunity.",
  "key_findings": [
    "21 splicing-derived peptides were detected via mass spectrometry on MHC-I in SLE patient neutrophils",
    "T cells expanded and secreted interferon-γ when exposed to these neoantigens",
    "SLE patient serum contained autoantibodies targeting novel amino acid sequences from splicing errors"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a mechanism by which aberrant mRNA splicing in lupus neutrophils directly generates autoantigens that initiate T and B cell responses, linking splicing dysregulation to autoimmune pathogenesis."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates bat mortality caused by wind turbines, focusing on operational adjustments to prevent deaths. The research assesses timing modifications to turbine operations as a mitigation strategy. Results indicate significant reductions in bat fatalities through strategic operational scheduling, highlighting a practical approach to minimize wildlife impacts without compromising energy production.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Adjusting wind turbine operation timing reduces bat fatalities",
    "Strategic scheduling of turbine operations prevents significant bat deaths",
    "Operational modifications offer a viable method to minimize wildlife impacts"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The findings provide a scalable, operational solution for reducing bat mortality from wind energy infrastructure, advancing conservation practices within renewable energy systems."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates Co/Co7Fe3 heterointerfaces for enhancing electrocatalytic nitrate reduction to ammonia. Using a dual-spillover mechanism, the catalyst achieves a near-unity Faradaic efficiency (99.16%) and high ammonia yield (36.07 mg h-1 cm-2) at -0.48 V vs RHE. The interfacial electric field optimizes water dissociation and proton supply, enabling efficient [4+4] tandem electron transfer pathways.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The Co/Co7Fe3 heterointerface enables a dual-spillover mechanism for nitrate reduction",
    "Near-unity Faradaic efficiency (99.16%) and high ammonia yield (36.07 mg h-1 cm-2) at -0.48 V vs RHE",
    "Interfacial electric fields optimize water dissociation and proton supply via hydrogen spillover"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a dual-spillover mechanism for efficient nitrate reduction, advancing electrocatalyst design principles for multi-electron reactions."
}
